+# Pass 9 app presentation requests
+
+Engine qualification does not establish these app-owned journeys. This is a
+handoff specification, not an implemented or tested UI change.
+
+1. Permissions: replace ChromiumRuntime's unconditional dismiss in
+   engine(_:permissionRequest:tab:) with a presenter routed by originating
+   AircTab/profile/window. Display origin, requested capability, Allow, Deny and
+   close. Resolve the request ID exactly once; close maps to dismiss. Honour
+   request-dismissed callbacks and dismiss on tab/profile/window changes. Anchor
+   to the real URL field using setUIAnchor(view:rect:), converting coordinates
+   only through the engine's uiAnchorRectInScreen. Test camera/microphone with
+   fake devices; test notifications/location independently. Verify allow and
+   deny, offscreen/background-tab suppression, and anchor geometry on resize.
+2. Passwords: subscribe to ChromiumEngine.passwordPromptDidChange and present
+   save/update at that same URL anchor. Use existing save/reject APIs and retain
+   originating tab identity. Do not log the password. Verify synthetic submit,
+   visible save, accept, reload, fill and isolation from the second profile.
+3. DevTools: ChromiumTab currently presents ChromiumToolsPanel. Provide explicit
+   dock/undock/re-dock state, lay out the page and tools together, preserve the
+   tools target across transitions, and test Option-Command-I through MainMenu.
+   Moving a native view alone does not prove Chromium's docking controls work.
+4. Add a bounded, nonactivating native qualification scenario to SnapshotRunner:
+   local fixtures, a small owned window, real Option-Command-U/I events, owned
+   CGWindowListCreateImage captures, print/PDF and upload panel selections, and
+   an unconditional shutdown/fixture cleanup path. The engine host's source URL
+   navigation is not an app shortcut test. App snapshots assembled from view
+   rendering are not evidence for these native surfaces.
+
+Native fullscreen and Japanese input-source switching need an interaction policy
+that preserves the owner's foreground app and input configuration. Do not enable
+an input source, take focus, or label those paths passed to unblock the table.
